\layout Standard

\SpecialChar ~


\layout ShortFoilhead


Example: Mean and Variance of Poisson Distribution
\layout Standard

As we mentioned in Section\SpecialChar ~
,
\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{sec:expectations}

\end_inset 

, the expectations under a distribution are important for summarising the
 distributions characteristics.
 Expectations of ditributions that take the form of a function can also
 be computed.
 Typically we expect the resulting expectation to be a function of the distribut
ions parameters.
\layout Standard

Let's start with the mean of the Poisson process.
 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle k\right\rangle _{P\left(k|\mu\right)}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}k\frac{\mu^{k}}{k!}e^{-\mu}\]

\end_inset 

 To make progress with this we first pull out 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu e^{-\mu}$
\end_inset 

 and the first 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 in the factorial, 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{k}{k!}=\frac{k}{k(k-1)!}=\frac{1}{(k-1)!}$
\end_inset 

.
 We can also remove the first term from the sum because it is multiplied
 by 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 which is zero for the first term.
\layout Standard

This leads to
\begin_inset Formula \[
\left\langle k\right\rangle =e^{-\mu}\mu\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{\mu{}^{(k-1)}}{(k-1)!}\]

\end_inset 

 Now we make the following substitution: 
\begin_inset Formula $m=k-1$
\end_inset 

.
 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\left\langle k\right\rangle =e^{-\mu}\mu\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\frac{\mu{}^{m}}{m!}\label{eq:poissonMean2}\end{equation}

\end_inset 

 Now we note that the geometric series 
\begin_inset Formula $\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\frac{\mu^{m}}{m!}=e^{\mu}$
\end_inset 

.
 Substituting this result back into (
\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{eq:poissonMean2}

\end_inset 

) we find 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\left\langle k\right\rangle =\mu\label{eq:poissonMean3}\end{equation}

\end_inset 


\layout Standard

The variance of a Poisson is also 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu$
\end_inset 

 --- see Tutorial 1.
 
\layout Standard


