Pollaczek-Khinchin formula
\layout Standard

If service times are general we cannot use birth death processes to analyse
 the system.
 
\layout Standard

Instead we derive the Pollaczek-Khinchin formula.
 This formula gives an expression for the expected waiting time in the queue
 for any distribution of service times.
 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\bar{W}=\frac{\lambda\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle }{2(1-\rho)}\]

\end_inset 

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{W}$
\end_inset 

 is expected waiting time, 
\begin_inset Formula $\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle =\left\langle X^{2}\right\rangle _{p(X)}$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho=\lambda\bar{X}$
\end_inset 

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{X}=\left\langle X\right\rangle _{p(X)}$
\end_inset 

.
 

