This means that to go via node 2 takes 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{1}{5}+\frac{1}{10}=0.3$
\end_inset 

 via node 3 takes 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{1}{13}+\frac{1}{5}=0.277$
\end_inset 

 via node 4 it takes 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{1}{14}+\frac{1}{14}=\frac{1}{7}=0.1429$
\end_inset 

 according to Kleinrock's independence assumption.
\layout Standard

Here we have assumed that there is no further delay associated with each
 link (propoagation, processing).
 In practice such delays may arise however we shall not consider them.
 See Bertsekas & Gallager Section 3.6.1 for more details.
